# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KERYX — local environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real values.
# Both values are public by design (they ship in the browser bundle); row-level
# security on the database is what protects the data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project: Settings > API in the dashboard.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side secrets. NOT read by the app; set them on the Supabase project
# (Edge Functions > Secrets, or `supabase secrets set`). Listed here so the
# full configuration is in one place.
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   required by the invoke-llm function (verse lookup,
#                       lyrics import, song search)
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL     optional, defaults to claude-opus-5-5
#
# Used only by scripts/migrate-from-base44.mjs (Base44 -> Supabase, web build).
# The desktop import (npm run db:import) needs only BASE44_APP_ID and
# BASE44_ACCESS_TOKEN:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL                same as VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   Settings > API > service_role — bypasses RLS,
#                               never put it in the browser or commit it
#   BASE44_APP_ID               the old app's id
#   BASE44_ACCESS_TOKEN         a logged-in Base44 session token
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
